  "notes": [
    "The diameter exponent is per material, not universal. PLA gains strongly with bore size (conduction and latent-heat limited); ASA barely gains (viscosity limited). A single exponent under-predicted high-flow PETG and ASA by 20-29%.",
    "highFlowResponse is applied only when the nozzle class is high-flow, and is normalised so PLA = 1.00.",
    "dryMaxC is a safe drying ceiling, NOT the glass transition. Semi-crystallines such as nylon are dried well above Tg and stay dimensionally stable; a Tg-based rule blocks correct practice and still permits spool-welding temperatures for PLA.",
    "Material constants outside PLA, PETG and ASA are polymer-family typicals, not measured values."
  ]
